{
  "example": "multi-resolution",
  "title": "Aligned grids at three resolutions",
  "package": "examples/valid/multi-resolution",
  "notes": [
    "All three grids share bounds, so their pixel edges nest (128 = 2 x 64 = 4 x 32).",
    "Elevation relative to sea level = value - 120 m. The derived sea-level pixel is floor((120+8000)/15000*65535 + 0.5) = 35476.",
    "precip-annual records its source resolution (128x64) and resampling (area_mean) separately from the delivered 32x16 grid."
